1
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:10,677
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,696
[objects clattering]

3
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,492
[sighs]

4
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:35,743
[Mickey] Fuck!

5
00:00:40,082 --> 00:00:41,541
Oh, shit!

6
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:46,213
[scrubbing]

7
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:49,883
Hey!

8
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:51,008
-Hi. Oh, no...
-Hi.

9
00:00:51,093 --> 00:00:52,385
-Don't step there.
-Oh, shit.

10
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:54,053
-[Mickey] I gotta sweep that up.
-Sorry.

11
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:58,266
Hey, did you notice last night,
there was a point where I was spooning you

12
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,061
[chuckles] and then
you were spooning Grandpa?

13
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:02,520
It was so cute.

14
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,147
Oh, my God!

15
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:06,483
Bertie leaves half-eaten
yogurt cups in here.

16
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:08,318
Who eats half a yogurt
and then puts it back?

17
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:10,528
She is a small person, so...

18
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,364
Can I help? Why are you cleaning?

19
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:16,618
Oh, well, my dad's coming to town,
so I figured I'd clean.

20
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:18,078
Your dad? Really?

21
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:21,831
Marty Dobbs, flying in from Jersey
as we speak.

22
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:24,584
Wow. I had no idea.

23
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:26,211
Well, he didn't tell me until yesterday.

24
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:27,962
My dad's Mr. Casual.

25
00:01:28,045 --> 00:01:30,965
But it's cool.
It'll be good to see him, I think.

26
00:01:32,175 --> 00:01:35,970
That's cool.
I'm sure you guys will have a fun time.

27
00:01:36,053 --> 00:01:37,305
-[Mickey] Hmm.
-Um...

28
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:40,809
you, uh, guys got any big plans?

29
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:43,728
[sighs] Well, I was gonna meet him
for lunch near the airport

30
00:01:43,811 --> 00:01:44,854
and bring him back here.

31
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,272
-Hmm.
-You should come with.

32
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:51,444
Oh! Uh, wow, okay, um...

33
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:53,029
-It'll be fun!
-[inhales sharply]

34
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:55,490
Please, please, please.
Free lunch on Marty Dobbs.

35
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:57,200
What else are you gonna do today, hmm?

36
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:58,285
I don't know. I just...

37
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:00,787
I don't wanna intrude on time
with your dad and...

38
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:04,374
Meeting a dad's kind of a big deal,
don't you think?

39
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:08,961
Dude, no. It is so not a big deal.
If you meet my mom, that's a big deal.

40
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:10,172
This will be easy.

41
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:13,466
My dad's kind of an asshole,
but you'll like him and he'll love you.

42
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,802
I mean,
compared to all the other guys he's met.

43
00:02:15,885 --> 00:02:18,012
The last guy was on cat tranquilizers.

44
00:02:18,095 --> 00:02:19,389
-Those work on humans?
-Yeah.

45
00:02:19,472 --> 00:02:21,308
Same as human ones.
You gotta take a bunch.

46
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:22,475
[chuckles]

47
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:26,521
So, what do you say, Cruikshank?
Are you in?

48
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,523
Uh...

49
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:29,524
okay.

50
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:31,067
Yes, fine.

51
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:34,237
Why not?
I'll meet Poppa Dobbs. Sure.

52
00:02:34,321 --> 00:02:36,948
Sweet! I'm gonna take a quick shower,
and we'll hit the road.

53
00:02:37,031 --> 00:02:38,158
Okay. All right.

54
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,167
Oh, hey, Gus.

55
00:02:48,751 --> 00:02:50,044
Bertie. Morning.

56
00:02:50,127 --> 00:02:51,671
Why is everything different?

57
00:02:51,754 --> 00:02:54,924
Oh, uh, Mickey's cleaning up. Yeah.

58
00:02:55,007 --> 00:02:56,551
I guess her dad's visiting.

59
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:57,468
-He is?
-Yeah.

60
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:59,929
And, uh, I'm gonna go meet him.

61
00:03:00,012 --> 00:03:01,848
-Oh, wow! For real?
-Mmm-hmm.

62
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:04,226
You think it's too soon?

63
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:08,020
Hmm. I don't know.
That's a good question.

64
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:12,150
-Oh, where'd my yogurt go?
-That's also a good question.

65
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:14,986
Do you know where it went?

66
00:03:15,737 --> 00:03:16,571
No.

67
00:03:19,491 --> 00:03:20,783
[music playing over radio]

68
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:23,578
-[Gus] You look nice.
-[Mickey] Glad I showered.

69
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:24,495
Oh, me too.

70
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,873
It would've been a bad first impression

71
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:29,208
to meet your dad with me,
like, reeking of sex.

72
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:30,335
-[Mickey] Hmm.
-[chuckles]

73
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:34,213
Yeah. That's probably something
dads can smell instinctively anyway.

74
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,298
[chuckling]

75
00:03:37,842 --> 00:03:41,554
Got any, uh, tips on meeting your dad?
Anything I should know going in?

76
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:45,850
-Mmm, not really.
-Yeah? What's he do for a living?

77
00:03:45,933 --> 00:03:47,894
He used to be a dentist,

78
00:03:47,977 --> 00:03:53,024
before he lost his license for giving out,
uh, prescriptions of pain medications.

79
00:03:53,107 --> 00:03:54,859
Oh. Okay.

80
00:03:54,942 --> 00:03:57,279
Now he's a consultant,
whatever that means.

81
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:59,614
-Hmm.
-He's always about to make a ton of money

82
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:02,492
on some amazing idea
that always falls through.

83
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:05,370
Uh, yeah, yeah.

84
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,789
When's the... when's the last time
you guys saw each other?

85
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:10,041
Two, three years ago.

86
00:04:10,542 --> 00:04:14,837
Oh. Shit. So this is...
this is kind of a big deal.

87
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:17,799
I mean, it's not not a big deal,
but it's not a big deal.

88
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:20,385
Do you two not...
Like, I don't know what...

89
00:04:20,468 --> 00:04:21,844
Do you guys not get along, or...

90
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:25,807
No, it's not that. I mean, we're just,
you know, both busy people.

91
00:04:25,890 --> 00:04:28,435
I mean, he's my dad,
so it'll always be a little complicated,

92
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:30,437
but we're not, like,
estranged or anything.

93
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,563
Yeah, yeah.

94
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:36,067
Well, don't worry,
dads are kind of my specialty.

95
00:04:36,984 --> 00:04:41,113
A lot of times an ex's dad will like me
more than his daughter ever did.

96
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:42,490
That's fucked up.

97
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:46,661
Yeah, I realize that's probably
not something I should brag about.

98
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:50,332
I'm guessing it's more of a turn on
to be the bad boy anyway, right?

99
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,583
Not for me anymore.

100
00:04:58,005 --> 00:05:00,925
Where is he? I mean, his plane landed,
like, an hour ago.

101
00:05:01,008 --> 00:05:04,387
Yeah. Uh, I wouldn't worry about it.

102
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:06,931
You know, it probably takes a long time
getting off the plane,

103
00:05:07,014 --> 00:05:08,516
and picking up your bags and...

104
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,643
waiting in line for those taxis and stuff.

105
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:13,980
-[Mickey] That's probably him.
-[Gus] Oh, yup.

106
00:05:15,648 --> 00:05:17,734
-Oh, shit.
-[Marty] Thank you.

107
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:21,153
-Hey, Dad!
-[chuckles] Hey, kiddo! How are ya?

108
00:05:21,237 --> 00:05:24,407
Aw. Man, you're even skinnier
than the last time I saw you.

109
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:26,576
[chuckles] Ah, you look
pretty good yourself.

110
00:05:26,659 --> 00:05:28,620
Yeah, I do, don't I? [chuckles]

111
00:05:30,246 --> 00:05:32,415
-Hello! Hi.
-Hey.

112
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:35,084
Sorry. This is Gus. He's...
Uh, we're dating.

113
00:05:35,167 --> 00:05:36,335
Nice to meet you, Marty.

114
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,839
-[chuckling]
-Sorry, I'm a hugger.

115
00:05:39,922 --> 00:05:41,048
-Gus, huh?
-Yeah.

116
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:44,761
I only ever knew one other Gus.
Gus Greenwold. Solid guy.

117
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:46,429
Oh, yeah.

118
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:49,682
I think I, uh, met him last year
at the, uh, Gus Convention.

119
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,684
He's not alive.

120
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:55,146
Oh. [chuckles] Um, I'm sorry.

121
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:58,232
Well, that's okay. I mean, at least
we're all still here, am I right?

122
00:05:58,315 --> 00:05:59,567
-Yeah!
-[both chuckling]

123
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:02,278
-Hey, can I take those for you?
-Uh, yeah.

124
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:03,738
Thank you. I mean...

125
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:06,240
-Eager little guy.
-Yeah.

126
00:06:07,199 --> 00:06:09,285
Isn't this place cool, Dad?
It's Himalayan.

127
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:11,370
They're supposed to have
the best samosas in LA.

128
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:14,957
Well, that's a bold statement, Mick.
You know how picky I am about my samosas.

129
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:16,167
[all chuckling]

130
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:18,920
So, uh, Marty, how was the flight?

131
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:20,337
[scoffs] Oh, my God.

132
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:24,217
They sat me next to a lady
with one of these therapy dogs.

133
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:27,136
You heard about this?
It's just a bullshit excuse for this lady

134
00:06:27,219 --> 00:06:28,971
-to bring her bichon everywhere.
-[chuckles]

135
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:31,766
I know. Therapy dogs. It's like, really?

136
00:06:31,849 --> 00:06:33,893
Right after we take off,
we hit a little turbulence.

137
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,061
This dog goes crazy.

138
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:38,815
Starts barking and whimpering
and immediately takes a dump...

139
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:39,899
-Oh, my God.
-on the floor.

140
00:06:39,982 --> 00:06:42,860
-No!
-It smells disgusting.

141
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:43,945
I mean, they clean it up,

142
00:06:44,028 --> 00:06:46,823
but for five full hours,
I am in dog shit hell.

143
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:48,783
People start looking at me
like it's my dog.

144
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:49,951
-That's awful!
-And I'm saying,

145
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:53,455
"Hey," you know, "Do I look like I'm
a fucking bichon owner to you?"

146
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:55,122
-No. You don't.
-[chuckling]

147
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:56,916
-You really don't... Yeah.
-Oh, thank you.

148
00:06:56,999 --> 00:06:59,001
Mick, you still got that cat?
What's his name?

149
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:02,672
Grandpa. 'Cause he's the reincarnation
of Grandpa, remember?

150
00:07:03,881 --> 00:07:06,884
Yeah. This is what makes Mickey Mickey.

151
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:07,969
[Marty and Gus chuckle]

152
00:07:11,388 --> 00:07:15,435
Oh, Dad, um, I got a promotion at work.

153
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:18,020
I'm a program manager now
at the radio station.

154
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:21,357
Really?
Hey, congratulations!

155
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,485
Hey, you always were good
at hustling up work.

156
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:25,903
-Thanks.
-You and me, huh? Both hustlers.

157
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:28,948
See, there's something good
you inherited from me.

158
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:30,032
It's in our blood.

159
00:07:30,908 --> 00:07:31,826
Right. Yeah.

160
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:33,578
[Gus chuckles]

161
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:36,539
[sighs] So, Gus, what's your last name?

162
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:38,583
-Cruikshank. Mmm-hmm.
-Cruikshank.

163
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:41,460
[chuckles] What nationality is that?

164
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:44,756
Oh, it's, um, Scottish. German.

165
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:48,134
Uh, you know, I... I gotta say,
I figured that you were maybe, uh--

166
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:50,094
-What? Jewish?
-Mmm-hmm.

167
00:07:50,177 --> 00:07:51,471
Ah! [chuckling]

168
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:55,016
Yeah, I get that sometimes.
'Cause of the, uh... [exclaims]

169
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:56,601
[both laughing]

170
00:07:57,351 --> 00:07:59,771
No, no, I was, uh,
I was actually raised Catholic.

171
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:02,064
-Well, you had me fooled.
-[chuckles] Good.

172
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:04,567
Gus was raised in South Dakota
and he teaches kid actors.

173
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:05,985
No kidding.

174
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:08,112
Have you ever heard of the show Witchita?

175
00:08:08,195 --> 00:08:09,656
Yeah, the witch show, you bet.

176
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,323
Gus worked on that show.

177
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:14,285
-And... he wrote a script for them.
-Ah...

178
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:17,496
-No! Hey, well, that's great!
-[Gus softly] Yeah.

179
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,456
Great.

180
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,000
Good for you, Micks.

181
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:24,170
Got yourself a nice, hardworking guy
with no tattoos or piercings.

182
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:25,337
[Mickey and Gus chuckle]

183
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:27,089
I had a feeling you two would get along.

184
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:28,340
Better than the last guy.

185
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:30,802
Remember when he fell asleep at the table?

186
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:32,887
-[Gus chuckles awkwardly]
-Have you decided?

187
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:35,765
[chuckles] Well, I've decided
that you are a ray of sunshine.

188
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:36,891
What's your name?

189
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:38,309
Pema.

190
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:41,395
Pema, beautiful Pema, huh?
How's your day?

191
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:44,106
-[Pema] It's good.
-Good, good.

192
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:48,861
Good, all right, well, we are gonna
start off with a couple orders of samosas.

193
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:53,741
And the tandoori shrimp,
uh, steamed momo,

194
00:08:54,241 --> 00:08:56,828
the lamb tikka masala...

195
00:08:58,287 --> 00:08:59,872
and the chicken vindaloo.

196
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:00,957
Good choices.

197
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,292
Uh, are you sure, Dad?
That's a lot of food.

198
00:09:03,375 --> 00:09:05,920
I live large.
Don't worry, lunch is on me.

199
00:09:06,504 --> 00:09:08,548
Hey, thank you.

200
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:11,133
So, uh, what brings you into town?

201
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:15,054
Oh, well, Southwest doesn't fly direct
to San Francisco from where I live.

202
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:17,932
But I'm heading up to Palo Alto.

203
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:20,267
Got a meeting with an investor I think
is going to help me out

204
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:21,518
with this new app I've got.

205
00:09:21,603 --> 00:09:24,480
Oh, okay.
What's the... what's the idea?

206
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:26,107
It's like Uber, but better.

207
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:28,943
[stutters] You know, it's the better Uber.

208
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:30,027
[chuckles]

209
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:33,906
These things are
all about right place, right time.

210
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:36,408
I mean, I've had guys rip me off,
make money off my ideas,

211
00:09:36,492 --> 00:09:38,410
but that is not gonna happen this time.

212
00:09:38,494 --> 00:09:42,665
Well, uh, I just wanna say, we're so glad
to have you in town and, uh,

213
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:45,001
maybe I'll get to find out
a little bit more about

214
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:46,878
what this one was like as a kid, huh?

215
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:49,756
-You got any, uh, funny stories?
-Oh, my God, where to begin?

216
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:53,259
-No. No, no.
-Oh, never mind. Forget it. Yeah.

217
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:55,678
-She ever tell you about the whip-its?
-Oh! Dad, come on.

218
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:58,055
Seventh grade.
Her mother has to pick her up from school,

219
00:09:58,139 --> 00:10:02,434
because she has been busted doing whip-its
in the parking lot at 11:00 a.m.

220
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:04,353
Mickey, you little scamp. [chuckles]

221
00:10:04,436 --> 00:10:05,688
That was a long time ago.

222
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:06,898
It was hard to punish her,

223
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:08,650
because we've all done whip-its, right?

224
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:11,861
[chuckles nervously] All the time.

225
00:10:11,944 --> 00:10:12,945
She ever tell you about the time

226
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:15,072
she got out of the car
in the middle of the night?

227
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:17,617
Uh, I don't think so,
but you don't have to... tell me.

228
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,410
So, I'm driving her home, right?

229
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:22,830
It's late. It's dark. I'm tired.
She's in the back. What are you, like, 13?

230
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:23,956
No, I was 11.

231
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,250
Either way, she will not stop complaining.

232
00:10:26,333 --> 00:10:27,543
I don't even remember
what she was talking about,

233
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:30,713
but she is bitching and moaning
and I finally just say,

234
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:33,424
"Hey, if you don't behave,
I'm pulling over."

235
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,843
-Classic dad move.
-But when I pull up at the light...

236
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:38,721
this kid gets out.

237
00:10:38,805 --> 00:10:40,597
That's not exactly
how I remember it, but--

238
00:10:40,682 --> 00:10:42,975
I am talking middle of the night,
Jersey City.

239
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:44,351
Homeless people, drunks.

240
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:46,312
God knows what kind of dangerous people
wandering around.

241
00:10:46,395 --> 00:10:48,314
I'm yelling at her,
"Hey, get back in here!"

242
00:10:48,397 --> 00:10:50,566
-[Gus chuckling]
-Of course, she doesn't listen.

243
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:54,779
So I spent the rest of the night
looking for her,

244
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:57,323
thinking she'd been kidnapped
or God knows what.

245
00:10:58,825 --> 00:11:02,161
And then I find her...

246
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:06,290
at a Burger King,
eating french fries and having a ball.

247
00:11:06,373 --> 00:11:09,210
-[chuckles]
-[Gus] Wow, that's a crazy story.

248
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:11,462
This one's always been
a little troublemaker.

249
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:14,966
We tell her to do something,
she does the opposite.

250
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,304
But that's what we love about her.

251
00:11:21,806 --> 00:11:23,390
[inhales deeply]

252
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:26,894
Lord knows she's had to put up
with my shit too, so... [chuckles]

253
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:31,733
Mmm.
Beautiful Pema, what have you got for us?

254
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:33,275
-Samosas...
-Mmm-mmm.

255
00:11:33,359 --> 00:11:34,401
That's good.

256
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:37,613
Oh, yeah! Looking good!

257
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:41,492
Yeah, I think I'm going to, uh,
go wash the airplane off my hands.

258
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:42,576
I'll be right back.

259
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:47,832
Fuck him.

260
00:11:49,625 --> 00:11:50,752
I'm so tired of his shit.

261
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:52,962
He loves telling
that stupid fucking story.

262
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:56,841
[sighs] I'm sorry. I feel like I'm the one
who told him to tell it, so...

263
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:59,176
You want to know
why I was so upset that night?

264
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,888
It's because I missed
my best friend's birthday party,

265
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:04,431
because I spent the whole day
sitting in the lobby of his office

266
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:07,351
while he pitched some shady business deal.

267
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:10,521
When he stopped the car,
he was yelling at me,

268
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:13,440
so when he told me to get out,
I thought he was serious,

269
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:15,567
because I was 11 years old!

270
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:19,822
So I got out and then he just drove away.

271
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:22,992
Oh, and he'll tell you that it was,
you know, just around the block.

272
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:25,578
But he fucking left me there.

273
00:12:25,661 --> 00:12:30,416
And I was just sitting there, by myself,
on the corner, in the dark,

274
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:32,668
for what felt like forever.

275
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:39,091
So I just walked to a Burger King
and sat in the corner and cried.

276
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:42,094
And I have never been
so scared in my life.

277
00:12:43,971 --> 00:12:45,890
[sighs]

278
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:47,516
Mickey, that's awful.

279
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:49,518
Yep.

280
00:12:50,937 --> 00:12:53,522
Look, I don't know
if this will make you feel better,

281
00:12:53,605 --> 00:12:56,818
but, you know, lot of times,
when we're kids,

282
00:12:56,901 --> 00:13:00,654
we feel things, like,
a little more severely than what's real.

283
00:13:00,737 --> 00:13:02,198
Are you taking his side?

284
00:13:03,365 --> 00:13:05,451
No, no. I'm just saying...

285
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:09,205
stuff like this is always,
like, super complicated, you know?

286
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:12,917
It's like that thing they say,
"It's corny, but it's true."

287
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,710
It's like our parents know
which buttons to push,

288
00:13:14,793 --> 00:13:15,920
because they're the ones
who installed them.

289
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:17,629
Dude, you don't have to fix everything.

290
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:19,966
Okay? Jesus! Whatever!

291
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:22,676
I just... All I ever wanted...

292
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,428
[sighs] Forget it.

293
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:26,388
[sighs]

294
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:28,599
[Marty sighs]

295
00:13:29,558 --> 00:13:32,144
All righty, let me at this food!

296
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:33,770
-[Mickey] Mmm.
-[Marty chuckling]

297
00:13:33,855 --> 00:13:34,856
Mmm.

298
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:40,361
A little bland.

299
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:47,659
[Gus] Well, that was excellent.

300
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,786
-Yes.
-Should I box this up?

301
00:13:49,871 --> 00:13:52,957
Oh, nah.
Here, uh... Here's the card.

302
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,458
-Thanks, Dad.
-Yeah, thanks, Marty.

303
00:13:54,541 --> 00:13:57,586
Yeah, well, I've had better vindaloo,
but I liked it okay.

304
00:14:00,965 --> 00:14:02,799
Do you wanna come back to my place?

305
00:14:02,884 --> 00:14:04,510
Get settled in?

306
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:05,594
Didn't you get my text?

307
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:07,596
-I don't think so.
-No?

308
00:14:07,679 --> 00:14:09,181
Oh, maybe it didn't go through.

309
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:10,599
No, uh, my plans changed.

310
00:14:10,682 --> 00:14:13,394
I'm on the 8:00 p.m.
to San Francisco tonight.

311
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:15,687
I figured I'd get up there early,
get a good night's sleep

312
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:16,855
before the big meeting.

313
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,525
Oh, okay.

314
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:23,487
I mean, don't you want to
just come see where I live?

315
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:25,572
It's the first nice place
I've ever lived in.

316
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:28,492
Oh, sweetheart, I came to see you,
not your place.

317
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:31,412
Do you really want to spend three hours
in a car,

318
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:32,997
driving across town?

319
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,166
I'd rather just, you know,
find some place.

320
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:37,501
We could sit and talk.
I'll see your place next time.

321
00:14:38,877 --> 00:14:40,587
Okay, yeah. That makes sense.

322
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:48,887
[inhales deeply]

323
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:50,681
All right, where to now?

324
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:52,891
Yeah, uh, what do you think, Mickey?

325
00:14:53,392 --> 00:14:55,144
Hey, let's get a drink, huh?
Celebrate.

326
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:56,478
-[Gus] Hmm.
-Celebrate what?

327
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:59,940
Us. [chuckles] Life. My new business.

328
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:03,527
All good things, huh?
What, do we need a reason to celebrate?

329
00:15:03,610 --> 00:15:07,031
Yeah, um, maybe we could go to that,
uh, donut place that's around here?

330
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:08,115
It's pretty awesome.

331
00:15:08,199 --> 00:15:12,286
They got all these crazy flavors,
like marshmallow and basil, but...

332
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:14,914
it's not gross like I'm making it sound.

333
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:17,041
[chuckles] I don't want a donut.
We just ate.

334
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:19,793
Right, right, right. Uh... [stammers]

335
00:15:19,876 --> 00:15:21,212
What about a museum?

336
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:24,090
There's an exhibit around here
that's about medieval torture devices.

337
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:27,551
-Could be really fun, I think?
-Yeah. Yeah, come on, you need a drink.

338
00:15:27,634 --> 00:15:28,635
-Over here.
-[Gus] Okay.

339
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:37,894
[door chimes]

340
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:42,024
[sighs] Hello.

341
00:15:42,984 --> 00:15:45,236
Uh, you guys grab a table.
I'll get some drinks, okay?

342
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:47,863
-[Gus] Okay.
-This place reeks.

343
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:51,617
-What's your name?
-Carol.

344
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:53,910
-Carol, huh? Beautiful Carol.
-Yes.

345
00:15:53,995 --> 00:15:55,662
-Ah...
-Marty Dobbs. How are you?

346
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:57,498
-Marty Dobbs, how are you?
-What are you drinking?

347
00:15:58,665 --> 00:16:01,293
I hate this.
I hate everything about this.

348
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:03,837
What... [sighs]
What am I doing in a bar?

349
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:07,008
Yeah. Are you okay?

350
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:09,051
You, um... You tempted or...

351
00:16:09,135 --> 00:16:11,720
No. I don't... [sighing]

352
00:16:11,803 --> 00:16:13,347
-I don't know!
-[laughing]

353
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:16,558
Well, here's to you, Jersey girl!

354
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:19,103
I don't wanna watch him drink
during the day. He's an alcoholic.

355
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,104
You think so?

356
00:16:20,604 --> 00:16:23,482
He got a DUI when I was in high school
and had his license suspended.

357
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:25,984
He had to go to court-mandated AA.

358
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:28,362
You know what, let's get out of here.
Tell him we wanna go.

359
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:32,574
No, let's just stay.
It's not worth it to piss off Marty Dobbs.

360
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:35,244
Whatever you need,
I'm here for you, okay?

361
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:37,371
Seriously.

362
00:16:37,454 --> 00:16:38,455
[Marty] Can you believe this?

363
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:41,833
You see that lady over there?
Her name's Carol.

364
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:45,546
She grew up two towns away from me
and here we are, meeting in a bar in LA.

365
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:47,131
-What are the chances of that?
-[glasses clink]

366
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:49,675
-Serendipity.
-All righty.

367
00:16:49,758 --> 00:16:51,843
Gussy, grab your glass!

368
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,264
Mickle the pickle. [sighs]

369
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:57,308
And one for the pops.

370
00:16:57,391 --> 00:17:01,062
Here's to my beautiful daughter
and to Gus.

371
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:03,021
Love you, Mick.

372
00:17:05,316 --> 00:17:07,651
Hey, come on, it's bad luck not to cheers.
Come on.

373
00:17:10,862 --> 00:17:13,031
Hey! All right.

374
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:16,243
I don't really feel like a beer,
so I'm gonna go smoke.

375
00:17:21,623 --> 00:17:24,543
I could never figure out that kid's moods.

376
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:26,878
[chuckles] God bless you, if you can.

377
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:29,590
Uh, I just try to listen.

378
00:17:29,673 --> 00:17:30,924
You should ask her how she's doing.

379
00:17:31,007 --> 00:17:33,427
I think, uh, it might turn things
around a bit.

380
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:37,473
I don't get it. I mean,
I come here, and she gets all quiet.

381
00:17:37,556 --> 00:17:39,475
[scoffs]
Won't even have a beer with her dad.

382
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:43,312
Hmm, well,
I wouldn't take it too personally.

383
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:46,815
I think she's, um...
She wants to, but...

384
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:48,650
What?

385
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:52,028
Well... she's sober.

386
00:17:52,821 --> 00:17:53,822
Sober?

387
00:17:53,905 --> 00:17:56,908
Yeah, like, um, you know,
in the... in the program.

388
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:59,787
-AA, huh?
-Yeah.

389
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:01,372
Again. [chuckles]

390
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:04,333
Well, good luck with that, Micks.

391
00:18:06,127 --> 00:18:07,503
I think it's really good for her.

392
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:34,238
-Sweetheart, can I bum a smoke?
-Sure. Here you go.

393
00:18:43,121 --> 00:18:46,375
-Best happy hour in the city, this place.
-That's awesome.

394
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,084
Three-dollar well drinks.

395
00:18:48,169 --> 00:18:51,129
Only problem is it doesn't start
for two more hours.

396
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:52,756
Carol got here too early.

397
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,384
[chuckles]

398
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:58,846
-I'm Carol. [snorts and laughs]
-Oh.

399
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:06,270
You got yourself a good daddy.

400
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:08,814
Oh, yeah, he's a real great guy.

401
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:11,983
He sure is.
He came all the way out here to see you.

402
00:19:14,486 --> 00:19:15,737
Lucky girl.

403
00:19:20,367 --> 00:19:23,454
Carol, your, uh, nipple's out.

404
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:26,665
Oh, whoopsies!

405
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:29,084
Whoops.

406
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:33,797
[music playing]

407
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:36,383
Hey, you know, Gus, I think I saw
a jukebox over there.

408
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:38,427
Why don't you go
pick us out some tunes, huh?

409
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,679
Oh, I don't want
to waste your money, Marty.

410
00:19:40,762 --> 00:19:42,431
Who knows how long it'll take
to play the song?

411
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:44,683
I'm not nervous.
Go for it, bud.

412
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:48,979
Uh... [exhales slowly] okay.

413
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:52,024
Cool. Be right back.

414
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:57,863
So, Mick?

415
00:20:00,198 --> 00:20:02,158
Gus told me something interesting.

416
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:03,702
Oh, what's that?

417
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:05,704
He says you're in AA.

418
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:08,707
He told you that?

419
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:11,668
Why would you do that to yourself again?

420
00:20:14,170 --> 00:20:15,422
Because I have a problem.

421
00:20:15,506 --> 00:20:17,799
AA is just a load of bullshit.

422
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:19,468
You know how I feel about this.

423
00:20:19,551 --> 00:20:22,638
[stammers] That is for people
that cannot think for themselves.

424
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:26,725
AA was started by a bunch of evangelicals
who were fuck-ups.

425
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:29,019
But they want to make us feel
like we got the problem.

426
00:20:29,102 --> 00:20:30,479
I don't have a problem.

427
00:20:30,562 --> 00:20:31,813
You don't have a problem.

428
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:33,482
They just want to make you think you do.

429
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:35,567
I am an alcoholic, Dad.

430
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,944
I need help.
AA is helping me.

431
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:39,696
Hmm. Yeah. All right, let me guess.

432
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,074
You go to the meetings
and you complain about your dad?

433
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:44,159
Is that it, huh?
It's all my fault?

434
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:46,620
-[Gus groans softly]
-Jesus, Mickey.

435
00:20:47,245 --> 00:20:49,790
I raised you to use your brain.
Not join a cult!

436
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:56,421
Hey, Marty, I just want to say...

437
00:20:57,464 --> 00:20:59,132
you have an amazing daughter.

438
00:20:59,215 --> 00:21:01,260
And you should be so proud of her.

439
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:03,429
Mmm. Thank you for saying that, Gus.

440
00:21:03,512 --> 00:21:04,972
That means a lot, coming from a guy

441
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:07,307
I hadn't even heard about
until an hour ago.

442
00:21:08,099 --> 00:21:11,437
Okay. All right.
Let's just take a breath here.

443
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:14,105
Gus, just stay out of it, okay? Jesus.

444
00:21:16,317 --> 00:21:17,318
[Marty] AA.

445
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:19,778
[scoffing] Oh, my God.

446
00:21:21,738 --> 00:21:22,823
Fuck.

447
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:34,584
[inhales deeply]
So tell me about your app, Dad.

448
00:21:35,085 --> 00:21:36,044
Well...

449
00:21:37,462 --> 00:21:40,674
it's called the R Car.

450
00:21:41,174 --> 00:21:44,136
It's a high-end car service
that comes and picks you up.

451
00:21:45,011 --> 00:21:46,472
So, it's exactly like Uber?

452
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:49,975
No. No, because you can reserve
your car in advance.

453
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:53,437
That's what the R stands for.
You can't do that with Uber.

454
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:56,482
Well, there are Ubers around all the time,
so you don't need to reserve them.

455
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:59,401
What about after a sporting event? Huh?
What about at the airport?

456
00:21:59,485 --> 00:22:02,321
I've never had to wait
for more than four minutes for an Uber.

457
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:05,031
We also have great cars.

458
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:08,994
They got bottles of water and mints
and iPhone jacks.

459
00:22:09,077 --> 00:22:11,413
You can charge your phone,
play your music.

460
00:22:11,497 --> 00:22:12,789
Yeah, Uber's got all of that.

461
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:18,170
And... and you can pick the kind of car
you want to get.

462
00:22:19,421 --> 00:22:22,215
Oh, that's cool.
So, could I get, like, a Ferrari?

463
00:22:22,298 --> 00:22:23,467
[chuckles]

464
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:26,387
Well, maybe not a Ferrari.
But, uh--

465
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,430
So it's exactly like Uber.

466
00:22:31,558 --> 00:22:32,726
[scoffs]

467
00:22:35,311 --> 00:22:36,312
[glass thuds]

468
00:22:38,774 --> 00:22:39,775
[chuckles]

469
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,903
Uh, you know what, I...

470
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:46,657
-I should probably get going. Yeah.
-[Mickey] Mmm.

471
00:22:47,616 --> 00:22:49,493
I gotta get back to the airport,
get checked in.

472
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:52,370
I might as well get there early.
Get situated.

473
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:55,374
Ah, but your flight's not
for another few hours.

474
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:59,377
Oh, no, no, no. You should go now.
Get situated. Uh, do you want a ride?

475
00:22:59,461 --> 00:23:01,171
-No, I'm fine.
-We should call you a taxi,

476
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:03,173
'cause you probably
wouldn't want to take an Uber, huh?

477
00:23:04,132 --> 00:23:05,426
That's a good one.

478
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:07,636
Yeah. I got to go square up.

479
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:25,361
How's Uncle Tim?

480
00:23:25,446 --> 00:23:26,572
[scoffs]

481
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:28,407
Still a fuck-up.

482
00:23:29,491 --> 00:23:31,618
[Gus] Here we go. Okay.

483
00:23:31,702 --> 00:23:33,369
Marty, let me give you these.

484
00:23:33,454 --> 00:23:34,913
-All right.
-Okay.

485
00:23:34,996 --> 00:23:36,373
Good luck up there!

486
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:37,874
-Thanks.
-Okay.

487
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:40,836
All right. Bye, Micks.
Don't be a stranger.

488
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:42,838
Love you.

489
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:45,882
[chuckles] I love you, too.

490
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:52,514
All right.

491
00:24:19,415 --> 00:24:20,416
[Mickey sighs]

492
00:24:21,502 --> 00:24:24,045
Why would you tell my dad that I'm sober?

493
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:27,382
Do you know how fucked up that is,
to break somebody's anonymity?

494
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:30,426
-To their dad?
-Okay. I was trying to help.

495
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:33,221
I didn't want your help.
Your help is not helping.

496
00:24:33,304 --> 00:24:35,724
I just wanted you
to be a buffer between us.

497
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,183
That's what I thought I was doing.

498
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:39,185
I wanted him to see I was grown up

499
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:42,438
and I had my shit together and maybe,
maybe he would just treat me differently.

500
00:24:42,522 --> 00:24:46,151
And we could have a decent day for once.
But it was the same thing.

501
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:48,529
It's always gonna be the same.

502
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:50,614
You don't know that.

503
00:24:50,697 --> 00:24:52,533
Things change.
People change.

504
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:55,160
I almost got through one day with him
without a fight.

505
00:24:55,243 --> 00:24:57,704
But then you had to go
and fucking tell him about AA

506
00:24:57,788 --> 00:24:59,289
and he got all pissed off.

507
00:24:59,372 --> 00:25:02,543
That is so fucked up, Gus!

508
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:04,460
I can't even be in a car
with you right now.

509
00:25:06,129 --> 00:25:08,757
Oh, my God...
Mickey, come on!

510
00:25:11,092 --> 00:25:13,261
-Jesus Christ.
-[door slams]

511
00:25:13,344 --> 00:25:14,470
[Mickey] Fuck.

512
00:25:14,555 --> 00:25:15,556
-Mickey, wait!
-[sighs]

513
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:17,641
Come on!
Come on, just wait. Hold on.

514
00:25:17,724 --> 00:25:19,434
[sighs] Oh, God.

515
00:25:19,517 --> 00:25:20,769
Just...

516
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:25,065
Do you really fucking need
people to like you that badly?

517
00:25:25,148 --> 00:25:27,483
I'm the one who should matter to you.
Not him.

518
00:25:27,568 --> 00:25:29,778
"Oh, Marty, you're so funny."

519
00:25:29,861 --> 00:25:32,405
[sighs] You should have stood up for me.

520
00:25:32,488 --> 00:25:34,908
I tried, but you told me to, like...

521
00:25:34,991 --> 00:25:37,077
-Oh, Jesus. Just stop it!
-It's very confusing for me.

522
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,912
You want me... your dad to like me.

523
00:25:38,995 --> 00:25:41,081
Am I supposed to have him hate me?
Do I... What?

524
00:25:41,164 --> 00:25:42,583
Shut the fuck up!

525
00:25:49,839 --> 00:25:52,717
I'm sorry. Okay? [sighs]

526
00:25:56,179 --> 00:25:57,180
[sighs]

527
00:25:58,849 --> 00:26:00,308
I know I messed up, and...

528
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:04,062
I'm truly sorry.

529
00:26:06,982 --> 00:26:08,149
I'm sorry too.

530
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:09,484
I'm... [sighs]

531
00:26:11,319 --> 00:26:13,154
It's really not you. It's him.

532
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:16,950
He was shitty to you.
It's okay to be upset.

533
00:26:20,912 --> 00:26:23,290
I'll give you a ride home
so you can get a break from me.

534
00:26:25,626 --> 00:26:27,252
I don't want a break from you.

535
00:26:32,882 --> 00:26:33,800
Okay?

536
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:35,593
[Mickey sighs]

537
00:26:47,188 --> 00:26:50,400
Oh, oh, oh!
Oh, my God, that could be my dad's plane.

538
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:51,609
Fuck you!

539
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:54,529
Yeah. Fuck you, Marty!

540
00:26:58,658 --> 00:27:00,619
['60s rock music playing]

